### Registration

Competitors interested in participating in **pkmn.ai**'s ladders or tournaments
can request inclusion [via
GitHub](https://github.com/pkmn/ai/issues/new?template=register.yml). You will
be required to provide:

- your **project's name** (max 18 characters, following Pokémon Showdown
  username conventions; subject to staff discretion, prefer regex
  `^[A-Za-z ]+$`, distinct from other projects, must not include the tokens
  `poke` / `mon` / `pkmn` / `AI` / `bot` / `agent` / `showdown` / `smogon`, bare
  English Pokémon species names, or known players' names)
- **GitHub and Smogon usernames** for each team member associated with your
  project. All authorized team members must be Smogon account holders in good
  standing.
- **Qualifying criteria** to justify participation in the hosted environment
  (_e.g._, [Pokémon Showdown](https://pokemonshowdown.com/ladder) /
  [vgc.bot](https://vgc.bot/leaderboard) /
  [pkmn.bot](https://pkmn.bot/leaderboard) rankings)
- descriptive fields on **project details** for the [projects](/projects)
  page
- agreement to:

  1. adhere to the latest community guidance on [Responsible Releases](/release)
  2. grant **pkmn.ai** permission to run your model in its arena for the purpose
     of evaluation against other agents
  3. grant **pkmn.ai** permission to run your model to aid evaluating suspected
     cheating cases in Smogon & Pokémon Showdown competitions

- A PNG image (_optional_) with your **project's logo** to be displayed on
  your project's statistics page

This will open up an issue on the [pkmn/ai](https://github.com/pkmn/ai)
repository. Staff will review this issue, fill in the appropriate information in
[`projects.yml`](https://github.com/pkmn/ai/blob/main/static/projects.yml),
and approve your project for submissions.

### Submission

Registered competitors may access the [account](/account) page which requires
GitHub OAuth credentials to authenticate. On this page you will be able to
manage account details (_e.g._, associating a Discord user ID with your account
to be used for notifications about your submissions and for roles within the
[chat](/chat) room) and view your account's status. Once your account is
approved and eligible for submissions you can fill out a submission form with
the following information:

- **`version`**: Version string (max 12 characters, _e.g._, `1.0.0` or `v2`,
  regex `^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,11}$`).
- **`download_url`**: Direct HTTPS URL to a `.tar.gz`/`.tar.xz`/`.tar.zst` bundle
  _or_ an OCI container image reference (_e.g._, `ghcr.io/...`, `docker.io/...`).
- **`sha256`**: 64-character hex SHA-256 checksum of the archive or OCI manifest
  digest.
- **`auth_token`** (_optional_): Read-only bearer token / header used once by the
  arena to pull private artifacts.
- **`ladders`** / **`tournaments`**: Non-empty subset of active ladders or
  scheduled tournaments to enter your agent in (submitted separately).

Ladder submissions run on an **Apple M6 Mac mini** with access to **10 cores** (8
Performance & 2 Efficiency), **14 GiB** of dedicated RAM, and **4 GiB** of scratch
`/tmp` storage wiped between games. The **network is disabled** for all
competitors. Ladder submissions may either take the form of an OCI `linux/arm64`
container or a native `darwin/arm64` bundle with native access to Metal/ANE/CoreML.
Tournament hardware is outlined in the tournament-specific rules and supports OCI
containers only.

{summary="**OCI Container**"}
::: details
```dockerfile
FROM --platform=linux/arm64 rust:1.85-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /src
COPY . .
RUN cargo build --release && strip --strip-unneeded target/release/my-agent

FROM --platform=linux/arm64 debian:bookworm-slim
COPY --from=builder /src/target/release/my-agent /usr/local/bin/my-agent
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/my-agent"]
```
:::

{summary="**Native Bundle**"}
::: details
```bash
mkdir -p dist/src dist/weights
uv python install 3.12
uv venv --python 3.12 --relocatable --no-cache dist/.venv
uv pip install --no-cache --python dist/.venv/bin/python mlx numpy
find dist/.venv -name '__pycache__' -type d -exec rm -rf {} +

cp src/*.py dist/src/
cp weights/*.safetensors dist/weights/

cat << 'EOF' > dist/run
#!/usr/bin/env bash
DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
exec "${DIR}/.venv/bin/python" -u "${DIR}/src/main.py" --weights "${DIR}/weights"
EOF
chmod +x dist/run
tar -czf agent-bundle.tar.gz -C dist .
```
:::

Every agent submission must occupy at most **500 MB of uncompressed resident
space** on disk once unpacked. Native bundles must contain at most 25,000
files/directories/symlinks and contain an executable `./run` at the archive
root. OCI containers must contain at most 32 OCI layers and the container
`ENTRYPOINT` / `CMD` must run the agent.

Tournaments accept 1 active entry per project (entries may be updated until
00:00 UTC before the start date). Ladder competitors may have **up to 2 versions**
of their project competing concurrently and may submit a new ladder version once
both of the following conditions hold:

- **14 days** have elapsed since their last successful ladder submission
- all of their **active ladder entries have settled** to $`\text{SE}(R) \le
  30\text{ Elo}` ($`\hat{\sigma} \le 0.173` nats, 95% CI $`\approx \pm 59\text{
  Elo}`) and at least 25 blind-pair matches (50 games)

A submission passes smoke testing if the arena can unpack the artifact and play
through Turn 1 of a battle in every selected format. On ladders, if 2 versions of
a project are already active when a 3rd passes smoke testing, the version with
the lower conservative rating ($`R - 1.96 \cdot \text{SE}`) is automatically
retired, retaining the **strongest version of the agent alongside the latest
submission**.

### Formats

Three permanent Constructed Singles ladders and two rotational ladders are hosted:

- **RBY** (`gen1ou`): Permanent Gen 1 OU (`harvested` private team pool).
- **ADV** (`gen3ou`): Permanent Gen 3 OU (`harvested` private team pool).
- **SV** (`gen9ou`): Permanent Gen 9 OU (`harvested` private team pool).
- **RAND** (`gen9randombattle`): Rotational Random Battle (`random` generated teams; full `.log` replays and `.tar` archives published).
- **VGC** (`gen9championsvgc2026regmc`): Seasonal VGC (`pools` competitor-submitted 20-team rosters; logs and `teams.json` remain private until the season is `archived`).

{summary="**RAND** (`gen9randombattle`)"}
::: details
Teams are generated per pair from a 256-bit CSPRNG seed and mirrored across Game 1 and Game 2 (swapping seats and teams in Game 2). Era-matched random-battle set/probability files (`data.json`, `full.json`, `sets.json`) are mounted read-only under `$PKMN_STATS_DIR/<ladder_id>/`.
:::

{summary="**VGC** (`gen9championsvgc2026regmc`)"}
::: details
Each entrant submits 20 legal teams passing a $`D(A, B) \ge 1.30` 1-nearest-neighbor uniqueness check against public reference pools and within the submitted batch. Once a version passes smoke testing, that 20-team roster is locked for the season. Matches require at least $`N \ge 4` active competitors and sample unordered team pairs so each entrant's roster appears with exact marginal probability $`2/N` and at most one of the two teams in any match belongs to either active player.
:::

Permanent formats freeze rules and mechanics to `@pkmn/sim` `v0.11.0` and are not mutated if community tiering changes later. Timers match Pokémon Showdown's `150s` bank (`+60s` Turn 1 grace, `+10s/turn` in Singles, `+25s/turn` in Doubles/VGC), except **choice cancellation and pondering are disabled** on ladders. Scheduled cloud-GPU tournaments may run distinct formats (such as Best-of-3 Open Team Sheets) with pondering enabled. Era-matched `@pkmn/stats` usage files (`stats.json`) are mounted read-only at `$PKMN_STATS_DIR/<ladder_id>/`.

### Matchmaking & Ratings

Every ladder match is a **2-game blind-pair mirror** (`Game 1` and `Game 2` with seats and assigned teams swapped under the same CSPRNG seed) to cancel team-matchup and Turn-1 seat variance. Pairings prioritize active-learning information gain for unsettled Challengers and top-of-ladder contention while avoiding repeated back-to-back pairings.

Standings are computed via **MAP Generalized Davidson** pairwise ratings over the 5 blind-pair outcome categories (`WW`, `WT`/`TW`, `WL`/`LW`/`TT`, `LT`/`TL`, `LL`), pinned to a designated `1500` Elo anchor and sorted by conservative lower confidence bound ($`\text{LCB} = R - 1.96 \cdot \text{SE}`). Agents that crash, time out, OOM, or exceed protocol strike limits forfeit the game and are automatically quarantined upon repeated consecutive faults.

### Packaging & Uploading Recommendations

{summary="**Packaging**"}
::: details
- Strip debug symbols from compiled binaries and shared libraries (`strip -x` on macOS, `strip --strip-unneeded` on Linux).
- Quantize neural network weights (`float16`, `bfloat16`, or `int8` `.safetensors` / `.gguf`).
- Pre-compile CoreML `.mlpackage` models to `.mlmodelc` (`xcrun coremlcompiler compile Model.mlpackage ./weights/`) and exclude intermediate build files.
- Exclude `__pycache__`, `.git`, test suites, `pip`/`uv` caches, C++ header files (`include/`), and static archives (`.a`).
:::

{summary="**Uploading**"}
::: details
- Upload `.tar.zst` / `.tar.gz` to a private Cloudflare R2, AWS S3, Backblaze B2, or GCS bucket and generate a presigned `GET` URL (`rclone link` or `aws s3 presign --expires-in 86400`).
- Host the bundle on a private GitHub repository release and pass a fine-grained PAT scoped strictly to that single repository with `Contents: Read-only`.
- Host the bundle in a private HuggingFace repository and provide a read-only token (`hf_...`) scoped to that repository.
- Push OCI containers to `ghcr.io`, `docker.io`, `quay.io`, Artifact Registry, or ECR and provide a temporary read-only pull token if private.
:::

---

### Protocol & Integration Guide

This section summarizes the protocol requirements and runtime invariants for adapting a Pokémon Showdown agent to the **pkmn.ai** Arena.

#### 1. Communication Over `stdin` / `stdout` (No WebSockets or Login)

- Standard Pokémon Showdown clients connect over WebSockets, authenticate via `|challstr|`, issue `/utm` and `/search`, and multiplex room IDs (`>battle-gen9ou-12345`).
- **In the Arena**, your agent is spawned as a fresh subprocess for **one single game** and communicates strictly over **`stdin`** and **`stdout`** with no room-ID prefix lines:

  - Read newline-delimited Showdown protocol lines from `stdin`.
  - Write a single newline-terminated choice line (`<= 64 KiB`, _e.g._, `move 1`, `move 2 terastallize`, `switch 3`, `team 123456`, or Doubles `move 1 +2, switch 3`) to `stdout` whenever you receive an active `|request|<json>` (where `request.wait` is falsy).
  - Write all diagnostic logging to `stderr` (never `stdout`, and plain-text chat is never forwarded to `@pkmn/sim` or your opponent).

#### 2. Assigned Teams via `|utm|<packed_team>`

- On ladders (and pre-assigned pool tournaments), the very first line written to your agent's `stdin` before `|init|battle` is:

  ```text
  |utm|<packed_team>
  ```

- **Do NOT use `line.split('|')[2]`**: Packed team strings use `|` internally between each Pokémon's 12 fields and `]` between Pokémon. Always slice after the 5-character `|utm|` prefix:

  ```typescript
  if (line.startsWith('|utm|')) {
    const packedTeam = line.slice(5);
    const myTeam = Teams.unpack(packedTeam);
  }
  ```

- Standard Showdown `|request|` JSON omits EVs, IVs, and Nature (providing computed `stats`, `moves`, `baseAbility`, `item`, and `teraType`). Parsing `|utm|` gives forward simulators exact EV spreads, IVs, Natures, and Hidden Power types before Turn 1. (In scheduled tournaments where entrants bring their own teams, zero lines are sent on `stdin` initially and your agent's first `stdout` line must be `/utm <packed_team>`.)

#### 3. Time-Slicing & Authoritative Turn Clocks

- Because both ladder agents share one M6 Mac mini, the Arbiter freezes your process group (`SIGSTOP` or `podman pause`) the instant your choice newline arrives on `stdout` and resumes it (`SIGCONT` or `podman unpause`) on your next decision prompt.
- **Wall-clock time jumps while paused**: Subtracting `Date.now()` / `clock_gettime()` across turns includes your opponent's thinking time while your process was frozen.
- Within a single turn, measuring elapsed time from reading `|inactive|Time left: ...` is accurate; across turns, always parse the clock line emitted immediately after each `|request|<json>`:

  ```text
  |inactive|Time left: 150.0 sec this turn | 150.0 sec total | 60.0 sec grace
  ```

#### 4. Flush Choices Immediately & Finish Bookkeeping Before `\n`

- The Arbiter pauses your process within microseconds of reading `\n` on `stdout`. Perform fast per-turn bookkeeping *before* printing your choice, and **flush `stdout` explicitly** (`sys.stdout.flush()`, `fflush(stdout)`, `println!`) so buffered stdio never stalls your turn timer.

#### 5. Handling `[Invalid choice]` vs `[Unavailable choice]`

- If your agent emits an illegal choice, `@pkmn/sim` keeps your turn clock running and sends:

  ```text
  |error|[Invalid choice] Can't move: ...
  |inactive|Time left: ...
  ```

  Emitting **3 consecutive `[Invalid choice]` lines** on the same request forfeits the game (`invalid-choice`).
- When hidden mechanics (such as `Encore`, `Disable`, or `Imprison` revealed at resolution) trigger `|error|[Unavailable choice]`, `@pkmn/sim` also emits a fresh updated `|request|<json>` revealing the newly restricted state without counting as an invalid-choice strike (capped at 16 total retries per turn).

#### 6. Statelessness, Read-Only Bundle & Scratch `/tmp`

- Each game spawns a clean process with its bundle directory (or container rootfs) mounted **read-only** and player display names anonymized (`Agent A` / `Agent B` — always read `request.side.id` `"p1"` or `"p2"`).
- A 4 GiB writable scratch volume is mounted at `$TMPDIR` (`/Volumes/P1` or `/Volumes/P2` natively, `/tmp` & `/scratch` in containers, also exposed via `$XDG_CACHE_HOME`) for shader/model caches and is **completely wiped** before and after every game.

#### 7. Format Selection, Hardware Limits & Read-Only `mmap()` Weights

- Only check ladders your agent implements; smoke testing runs a Turn-1 game in **every selected ladder** (failed smoke tests automatically refund the 14-day submission cooldown).
- **CPU Threads (`10`)**: The Arena exports `OMP_NUM_THREADS=10`, `MKL_NUM_THREADS=10`, `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=10`, `VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=10`, `NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=10`, `TORCH_NUM_THREADS=10`, and `RAYON_NUM_THREADS=10`. Do not hardcode thread pools above 10 threads.
- **Unified Memory (`14 GiB` / `14,336 MiB`)**: Enforced across CPU RAM + Metal GPU + ANE (`ARENA_MEMORY_LIMIT_MB=14336`). Keep search tables within $`\le 8\text{–}10\text{ GiB}` to leave headroom for runtime allocations.
- **Zero-Footprint Model Weights via Read-Only `mmap()` (Native Bundles)**: `/opt/arena/bin/limit` enforces the 14 GiB cap via XNU's `ri_phys_footprint`. Clean, read-only file-backed pages (`mmap` with `PROT_READ` on `.safetensors` or `.gguf` weights inside the read-only bundle) count as **0 bytes toward `ri_phys_footprint`** and start in $`< 5\text{ ms}` once warm in the unified buffer cache.
